    "domain": "super-Hubble (k eta_B << 1), linear-order transfer of the curvature perturbation, single-clock adiabatic matter contraction with a > 0 throughout, geometric prescription z = a (c_s = 1), symmetric or matched bounce with bounded a''/a.",
    "computed": "(a) T_c(k) = 1 for a pure constant-branch IC (phase-3 reproduced in three backgrounds); (b) the adiabatic vacuum is growing-branch dominated, |r| = 9 A^2 I_inf/k^3; (c) the k-independent super-Hubble rescaling lambda between the NEC boundary and late times, hence the LINEAR-TRANSFER transmission coefficient T_fNL = 1/lambda = (1 - rho_B)/2 with rho_B = |J(-eta_B)|/I_inf.",
    "NOT_computed": "the bounce's OWN cubic (in-in) contribution Delta f_NL^bounce from the third-order action during NEC violation. Quintin et al. 2015 (arXiv:1508.04141) find f_NL is ENHANCED during the bounce phase when zeta grows; Agullo, Bolliet & Sreenath 2017 (arXiv:1712.08148) find the LQC bounce enhances non-Gaussianity by several orders of magnitude on scales larger than the curvature radius at the bounce. That term has the OPPOSITE sign of effect to the suppression computed here and is NOT bounded by it: the net T_fNL is therefore NOT determined by the linear transfer alone."
